WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
而且我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了这档《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:34.400
Four score and seven years ago, our fathers brought forth on this continent a new nation.
八十七年前，我们的先辈在这片大陆上建立了一个新国家。

9
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:42.040
Conceived in liberty and dedicated to the proposition that all men are created equal.
它孕育于自由之中，并致力于实现人人生而平等的理念。

10
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.980
Welcome, everybody, to Gettysburg.
欢迎大家来到葛底斯堡。

11
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.280
It is Season 8, Episode 8.
这是第八季第八集。

12
00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.680
Written by Robert Padnick and directed by Jeffrey Blitz.
由罗伯特·帕德尼克编剧，杰弗里·布里茨执导。

13
00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.500
Well, Ms. Lincoln, would you like to read us a summary?
那么，林肯女士，你愿意为我们读一下剧情梗概吗？

14
00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.060
Yes, please.
好的，没问题。

15
00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:04.160
Andy is struggling to inspire his—I'm kidding.
安迪正努力激励他的——我开玩笑的。

16
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.700
He's struggling to inspire his employees.
他正努力激励他的员工们。

17
00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:11.500
So he decides to take them on a corporate retreat to the Gettysburg Museum.
于是他决定带他们去葛底斯堡博物馆进行公司团建。

18
00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.180
He even has custom hats made.
他甚至还定制了帽子。

19
00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:21.020
The employees who choose to stay at The Office are recruited by Robert California to brainstorm innovative game changers.
选择留在办公室的员工被罗伯特·加州招募，去进行创新性的头脑风暴。

20
00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:23.780
And guess who gets Robert's attention?
你猜是谁引起了罗伯特的注意？

21
00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:25.220
Kevin.
凯文。

22
00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:26.720
Kevin the cookie man.
饼干人凯文。

23
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:27.260
Yeah.
没错。

24
00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.500
Much to Ryan's dismay.
这让瑞安非常沮丧。

25
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.040
I know.
我知道。

26
00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:32.660
He's just going to have to be the hot guy now.
他现在只能当那个帅哥了。

27
00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:34.320
Fast fact number one.
第一个速递事实。

28
00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.640
This is a location breakdown.
这是一次取景地解析。

29
00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.240
Fan question from Elise W.
来自Elise W.的粉丝提问。

30
00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:41.020
in Gettysburg, Pennsylvania.
关于宾夕法尼亚州的葛底斯堡。

31
00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.480
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

32
00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:50.720
Elise says, I have been waiting since the start of this podcast to write in about this episode because I grew up in Gettysburg, Pennsylvania,
Elise说，从这个播客开播起，我就一直等着写信问这一集，因为我是在宾夕法尼亚州的葛底斯堡长大的，

33
00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.920
and this little town was absolutely tickled that we were chosen to be featured in this amazing sitcom.
我们这个小镇对于能被这部精彩的情景喜剧选中感到非常兴奋。

34
00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:59.700
I know I can speak for the town when I say we were honored.
我代表全镇人民说，我们深感荣幸。

35
00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:05.580
Elise goes on to say, it is obvious that the scenes located in Gettysburg were not actually filmed there.
Elise接着说，很明显，在葛底斯堡的场景并不是真的在那里拍摄的。

36
00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:06.260
Oh, Elise.
噢，Elise。

37
00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:07.060
I'm so sorry.
我很抱歉。

38
00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.600
I would love to hear a location breakdown.
我很想听听取景地解析。

39
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:19.720
I would also love to know if anyone from the cast or crew came to Gettysburg or if you were able to get donations from local businesses or tour our historic town.
我也很想知道是否有演职人员去过葛底斯堡，或者你们是否从当地企业获得过捐赠，又或者参观过我们这座历史名城。

40
00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.780
Please, ladies, add the Gettysburg National Battlefield to your list of tourists to take.
女士们，请把葛底斯堡国家战场列入你们的旅游清单吧。

41
00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:32.560
It is a beautiful area with an amazing history and wonderful people that all, including myself, would love to show you around.
这是一个美丽的地区，有着令人惊叹的历史和美好的人民，包括我在内的所有人，都非常乐意带你们四处看看。

42
00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:34.520
I'm adding it to our liSt.
我把它加进我们的清单了。

43
00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.040
Our list is getting really long.
我们的清单变得越来越长了。

44
00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:37.940
It's going to require a lot of travel.
这需要大量的旅行。

45
00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:47.300
But I'm really looking forward to the season of my life where I am just kind of an older gal that gets to, like, go to fun places with my best friend.
但我真的很期待我人生中的那个阶段，那时我只是个老太太，可以和最好的朋友一起去有趣的地方玩。

46
00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.040
You're literally describing my mom and dad.
你描述的简直就是我爸妈。

47
00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.580
That is what they do.
他们就是那样做的。

48
00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:56.440
They travel around to different places in the United States and abroad.
他们在美国各地和国外旅行。

49
00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:57.920
Little nuggets.
小趣事。

50
00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.600
Not the big hits.
不是什么大新闻。

51
00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.920
They go to the little charming places.
他们会去那些迷人的小地方。

52
00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:05.080
Yeah, they're always finding some little nugget somewhere.
是啊，他们总能在某处发现一些小宝藏。

53
00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:10.500
Well, Elise, we shot the Gettysburg scenes at Woodley Park in Van Nuys.
嗯，埃莉斯，我们在范奈斯的伍德利公园拍摄了葛底斯堡的场景。

54
00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:15.060
The museum and archives were sets that we built on our warehouse stages.
博物馆和档案馆的场景是我们自己在仓库摄影棚里搭建的。

55
00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:20.640
Our design team did a lot of research to try and make the park look like the real Gettysburg.
我们的设计团队做了大量的研究，试图让公园看起来像真正的葛底斯堡。

56
00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:26.540
For example, Pam Punch, who was our NBC executive, grew up around Gettysburg and said,
例如，我们的NBC主管帕姆·潘奇，她是在葛底斯堡附近长大的，她说，

57
00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.000
Hey, it looks pretty good.
嘿，看起来还挺像那么回事的。

58
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.020
She gave some notes.
她给出了一些建议。

59
00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.580
Our art department brought in the cannons.
我们的美术部门运来了大炮。

60
00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:37.000
They brought in the signage and other kind of decorations to look like Gettysburg.
他们运来了标识牌和其他装饰品，让这里看起来像葛底斯堡。

61
00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:42.480
And Phil Shea got a bunch of stuff from the actual Gettysburg Battlefield National Park gift store.
菲尔·谢伊从真正的葛底斯堡国家军事公园礼品店买了一堆东西。

62
00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.500
Well, I reached out to Michael Gallenberg.
嗯，我联系了迈克尔·加伦伯格。

63
00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.100
You guys have heard us talk about him before.
你们之前听我们提起过他。

64
00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.560
He was our production designer.
他是我们的美术指导。

65
00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:51.640
And I wanted to know if he had any stories about putting this episode together.
我想知道他有没有关于制作这一集的故事。

66
00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:53.600
He emailed me back right away.
他很快就给我回了邮件。

67
00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:58.340
And he said, You know, Angela, Gettysburg was the end of my tenure on The Office.
他说，你知道吗，安吉拉，葛底斯堡是我在《办公室》任期的终点。

68
00:03:58.980 --> 00:03:59.280
Wow.
哇。

69
00:03:59.460 --> 00:03:59.700
Yeah.
是啊。

70
00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.180
He said, In fact, it might have been my last official episode.
他说，事实上，这可能是我最后参与的一集。

71
00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:07.140
So Michael actually put me in touch with Matt Flynn from the design team.
所以迈克尔实际上帮我联系了设计团队的马特·弗林。

72
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:10.360
And he had such fun things to share about this episode.
他分享了关于这一集非常有趣的事情。

73
00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:10.880
Ooh.
噢。

74
00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:11.760
Like what?
比如什么？

75
00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:15.920
Okay, first of all, he says, Greetings to you both, Jenna and Angela.
好的，首先，他说，向你们两位，珍娜和安吉拉问好。

76
00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:19.020
And congratulations on your very popular podcaSt.
祝贺你们的播客大受欢迎。

77
00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:19.660
Yay!
耶！

78
00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:20.660
Isn't that so sweet?
这不是很贴心吗？

79
00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:20.980
Yes.
是的。

80
00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:22.660
Great way to start an email to us.
给我们发邮件的绝佳开场白。

81
00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:29.080
And then he went on to say, Yes, indeed, this episode was my first stint as production designer at The Office.
然后他继续说，没错，这一集确实是我在《办公室》担任美术指导的第一次任务。

82
00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:34.420
However, he had been working with Michael Gallenberg as art director since season two.
不过，他从第二季开始就一直作为艺术总监与迈克尔·加伦伯格合作。

83
00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:34.960
Okay.
好的。

84
00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:35.980
I remember him.
我记得他。

85
00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:37.480
Yeah, he knew the show very well.
是啊，他非常了解这部剧。

86
00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:41.840
He shared one of the demands of the script was to provide a, ready for this?
他分享说剧本的要求之一是提供一个——准备好了吗？

87
00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:43.760
Here was his call to action.
这是他的行动号召。

88
00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:46.380
We need you to provide for us a verdant setting,
我们需要你为我们提供一个绿意盎然的环境，

89
00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:55.540
which has a parking lot adjacent to a plaza-like area in front of an existing structure where we could then turn it into a Gettysburg visitor center.
旁边要有一个停车场，连接着现有建筑前的一个广场区域，这样我们就能把它变成葛底斯堡游客中心。

90
00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:56.420
Wow.
哇。

91
00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.940
So, Jenna, you mentioned there were cannons, right?
所以，珍娜，你提到了有大炮，对吧？

92
00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:00.400
Yeah.
是的。

93
00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.480
He said they did a lot of research.
他说他们做了很多研究。

94
00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:04.980
They wanted to place them the way they were in the actual park.
他们想按照公园里的实际位置来摆放它们。

95
00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:09.140
And they had to rent these cannons from a prop house.
而且他们必须从道具店租这些大炮。

96
00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:09.980
Crazy.
太疯狂了。

97
00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.040
Listen to this.
听听这个。

98
00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:20.160
He said when they went to rent them, some of the cannons were in a distressed state and they required cosmetic repair because the prop house said, You know,
他说当他们去租的时候，有些大炮处于破损状态，需要进行外观修复，因为道具店说，你知道吗，

99
00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.280
these were used and gone with the wind.
这些可是《乱世佳人》里用过的。

100
00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:23.080
What?
什么？

101
00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:24.040
Yes.
是的。

102
00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:28.660
He went on to say that the prop rental house had a historic inventory.
他接着说，那家道具租赁公司有着历史悠久的库存。

103
00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:35.000
Now, you can't always 100 percent, like, be accurate about where they were used and everything,
当然，你不能百分之百确定它们具体是在哪里用过的，以及所有细节，

104
00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:41.240
but apparently the lore of these cannons were that they were the same ones used in the movie Gone with the Wind.
但据说这些大炮的传说就是它们和电影《乱世佳人》里用的是同一批。

105
00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:42.080
Wow.
哇。

106
00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:43.620
They kept those a long time.
他们保留了那么久啊。

107
00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:53.740
He also said one of the things he remembers is the existing structure that they made to look like the Gettysburg visitor center was actually a public restroom.
他还说他记得的一件事是，他们为了看起来像葛底斯堡游客中心而搭建的现有建筑，其实原本是个公共厕所。

108
00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:55.520
I wondered.
我当时就纳闷。

109
00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:56.880
I have to be honest with you.
老实跟你说吧。

110
00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:58.560
It had restroom qualities.
它确实有厕所的特质。

111
00:05:58.840 --> 00:05:59.380
Did it really?
真的吗？

112
00:05:59.460 --> 00:05:59.840
Yes.
是的。

113
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.280
When I saw it in the episode, I thought, Is that a bathroom?
我在剧集里看到它的时候，心想，那是个厕所吗？

114
00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:05.200
He said that, you know, covered it.
他说，你知道，他们把那儿遮住了。

115
00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.100
And then right as you enter, they built sort of like a fake wall.
就在你进去的地方，他们建了一堵假墙之类的东西。

116
00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:12.240
But if you went just around the corner, there was a row of toilets.
但如果你绕过拐角，那里有一排厕所。

117
00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:15.880
That is so funny because, you know, Angela, you and I weren't there.
这太搞笑了，因为，你知道，安吉拉，你和我当时不在那儿。

118
00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:17.120
We stay back at the office.
我们留在办公室里。

119
00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:19.500
So I love all that detail.
所以我很喜欢这些细节。

120
00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:25.420
I did find in an early draft that we were sent of the table read that my character went.
我确实在发给我们的剧本围读初稿里发现，我的角色去了。

121
00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:26.400
You went?
你去了？

122
00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:26.860
Yeah.
是啊。

123
00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:28.880
What did you do the whole time?
那你全程都在干什么？

124
00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:29.840
I don't know.
我不知道。

125
00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:30.340
Be miserable?
在那儿受罪？

126
00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:30.900
Yes.
是的。

127
00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:34.060
But I guess someone changed their mind, and I'm so glad.
但我猜有人改变了主意，我真庆幸。

128
00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:39.920
Because it meant, A, I got to be with you, and I got to be in an air-conditioned room for the whole week because it was hot.
因为这意味着，第一，我可以和你在一起，第二，我可以在有空调的房间里待上一整周，因为当时天气很热。

129
00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.320
Well, I loved that.
嗯，我喜欢那样。

130
00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.000
I'm so glad he got back with you.
我很高兴他回到你身边了。

131
00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:43.640
Thank you, Matt.
谢谢你，马特。

132
00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:44.340
I know.
我知道。

133
00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:52.580
Well, fast fact number two, I thought we could use a teeny tiny history lesson on the Battle of Gettysburg.
好吧，第二个冷知识，我想我们可以来上一堂关于葛底斯堡战役的小小历史课。

134
00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:53.160
Okay.
好的。

135
00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:56.760
That was fought July 1st through 3rd, 1863.
那场战役发生在1863年7月1日至3日。

136
00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:00.580
You know, just because we're there in the episode.
你知道，就因为我们在剧集里去了那里。

137
00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.760
All right, Professor Fisher, continue.
好吧，费舍尔教授，请继续。

138
00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:03.880
Here it is.
这就来了。

139
00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:08.420
The Battle of Gettysburg was led by Union Army General George Meade.
葛底斯堡战役由联邦军将军乔治·米德指挥。

140
00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:11.380
And this is the battle that ended the Civil War.
这就是结束了内战的那场战役。

141
00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:17.380
The Gettysburg National Cemetery and Gettysburg National Military Park are maintained by the U.S.
葛底斯堡国家公墓和葛底斯堡国家军事公园由美国国家公园管理局维护。

142
00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:18.680
National Park Service.
国家公园管理局。

143
00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:25.500
And four months after this battle is when President Abraham Lincoln delivered the famous Gettysburg Address.
在那场战役四个月后，亚伯拉罕·林肯总统发表了著名的《葛底斯堡演说》。

144
00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:28.940
You know, the one that begins the four score and seven years ago.
你知道的，就是那篇以“八十七年前”开头的演说。

145
00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:35.600
And that address also contains the famous line, quote, government of the people by the people for the people.
那篇演说还包含了那句名言：“民有、民治、民享的政府”。

146
00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:38.980
Gettysburg is located in Adams County, Pennsylvania.
葛底斯堡位于宾夕法尼亚州的亚当斯县。

147
00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:43.420
And it's about two hours and 45 minutes away from Scranton.
距离斯克兰顿大约两小时四十五分钟车程。

148
00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:45.920
So they would have had time to watch Limitless.
所以他们应该有时间看完《永无止境》。

149
00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:51.060
Oh, well, I've got a whole lot to say about this time on the bus later.
哦，关于这次坐巴士的时间，我之后还有很多话要说。

150
00:07:51.640 --> 00:07:57.860
But basically, yes, Andy made everyone spend six hours round trip on that bus that day.
但基本上，没错，安迪那天让每个人在那辆巴士上往返花了六个小时。

151
00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:02.740
Angela, for when we go visit the Gettysburg National Military Park, it is open year-round.
安吉拉，关于我们去参观葛底斯堡国家军事公园的事，它全年开放。

152
00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:05.560
And you can tour the park by walking.
你可以步行游览公园。

153
00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.280
You can drive your car.
也可以开车。

154
00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:10.960
They have, like, audio tours that you can download on an app.
他们有那种可以在应用上下载的语音导览。

155
00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:13.060
You can do it by bus.
你可以坐巴士游览。

156
00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:14.240
Or horse.
或者骑马。

157
00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:15.440
Please tell me horse!
请告诉我选骑马！

158
00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:16.300
Yes!
好啊！

159
00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:17.340
Yes, lady!
没错，女士！

160
00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:19.140
We have to do it by horse.
我们一定要骑马游览。

161
00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:22.120
A hundred percent we have to do it by horse.
百分之百，我们必须骑马。

162
00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:24.840
That just moved up higher on my liSt.
这在我的愿望清单上排名又上升了。

163
00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:25.380
Yeah.
是啊。

164
00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:25.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

165
00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:29.500
If you can tour it by horse, it gets priority billing.
如果能骑马游览，那绝对是首选。

166
00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:30.800
So there you go.
所以就是这样。

167
00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.120
That's a little bit about Gettysburg.
关于葛底斯堡就介绍到这里。

168
00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:40.120
Fast fact number three is a crazy, weird thing that Steve Burgess told me happened while
第三个冷知识是一件疯狂又奇怪的事，史蒂夫·伯吉斯告诉我，就在

169
00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.520
we were shooting this episode.
我们拍摄这一集的时候发生的。

170
00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:42.560
And you wouldn't tell me.
而且你还不肯告诉我。

171
00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.360
You said, I'm going to surprise you on the podcaSt.
你说，要在播客里给我个惊喜。

172
00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:45.000
So what?
所以到底是什么？

173
00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:46.820
I have photos.
我有照片。

174
00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:47.580
What?
什么？

175
00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:51.400
Meredith's van was struck by lightning.
梅雷迪思的货车被闪电击中了。

176
00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:52.020
What?
什么？

177
00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:53.860
In our parking lot.
就在我们的停车场里。

178
00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:54.340
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

179
00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:55.140
And it caught on fire.
而且还着火了。

180
00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:56.320
No way.
不会吧。

181
00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:56.840
Yeah.
是真的。

182
00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:58.800
Does Kate know that?
凯特知道吗？

183
00:08:58.820 --> 00:08:59.600
I don't know.
我不知道。

184
00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:00.880
We have to tell her.
我们得告诉她。

185
00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:01.840
Yeah.
是啊。

186
00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:05.100
The photo is like a burned out shell of a van.
照片看起来就像一辆烧焦的货车空壳。

187
00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:06.520
Holy crap.
天呐。

188
00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:08.280
He said they repaired it.
他说他们把它修好了。

189
00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:12.620
I thought it looks like a goner to me, but they repaired it.
我觉得它看起来已经报废了，但他们居然修好了。

190
00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:14.660
I mean, it was a pretty junky looking van.
我是说，那本来就是一辆看起来很破旧的货车。

191
00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:19.560
So maybe it having a little lightning distressing wasn't the worst thing.
所以也许被闪电劈出点做旧效果也不是什么坏事。

192
00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:20.280
No.
没错。

193
00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:22.900
There's like a giant fire hole.
上面有个巨大的火烧洞。

194
00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:24.100
Oh, my God.
天哪。

195
00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:25.840
In the whole top of the car.
在车顶上。

196
00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:28.720
In the whole top of the van.
在整个货车顶部。

197
00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:29.400
A fire hole.
一个火烧洞。

198
00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:32.720
I think that's what the, I think that's the technical term for it.
我想这就是，我想这就是它的专业术语。

199
00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:33.160
Come on.
得了吧。

200
00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:33.740
No, I'm kidding.
不，我开玩笑的。

201
00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:34.260
I don't know.
我不知道。

202
00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:39.980
But he said that our crew was actually at the technical Emmys.
但他提到我们的剧组当时其实是在技术艾美奖现场。

203
00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:41.380
Remember the technical Emmys?
还记得技术艾美奖吗？

204
00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:42.360
How much fun we have?
我们玩得有多开心？

205
00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:42.560
Yes.
是的。

206
00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:47.320
So the technical Emmys are the weekend before the Emmys, and it's where they give Emmys to
技术艾美奖是在艾美奖颁奖典礼的前一个周末举行，那是专门颁发给

207
00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:53.160
all of the crew members, editing, sound design, sort of all of those things.
所有剧组成员、剪辑、音效设计等这类幕后人员的奖项。

208
00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:58.760
And so our crew was attending the Emmys when they got a phone call that Meredith's van was
所以我们的剧组当时正在参加艾美奖，结果接到电话说梅雷迪思的货车

209
00:09:58.760 --> 00:09:59.480
on fire.
着火了。

210
00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:02.560
That's so crazy.
那太疯狂了。

211
00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:02.880
Yeah.
是啊。

212
00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:07.920
There was so much crap in that van, too, that they just left in there, like set decorating,
那辆车里还有好多乱七八糟的东西，他们就直接留在里面了，比如布景装饰，

213
00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:09.780
but it was like Meredith's mess.
但那简直就是梅雷迪思的烂摊子。

214
00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:13.680
I mean, what did the fire department think when they came to put that thing out?
我是说，消防队赶去灭火时会怎么想？

215
00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:14.660
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

216
00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:15.440
Yep.
没错。

217
00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:16.700
That is amazing.
那真是太绝了。

218
00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:18.260
I will be sharing those pictures.
我会把那些照片分享出来的。

219
00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:19.420
You have to send them to me.
你一定要发给我。

220
00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:20.340
I absolutely will.
我绝对会发的。

221
00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:22.700
Well, that's all I got for Fast Facts.
好了，这就是我准备的“快速事实”全部内容了。

222
00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:24.560
I loved your Fast Facts.
我很喜欢你的“快速事实”。

223
00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:25.300
And you know what?
你知道吗？

224
00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:26.320
Let's take a break.
我们休息一下。

225
00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:31.000
And when we come back, Gabe is holding a real boring meeting in the conference room.
等我们回来，盖博正在会议室里开一个超级无聊的会。

226
00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:44.360
We are back, and we're in the conference room.
我们回来了，现在在会议室里。

227
00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:46.380
Gabe is leading a meeting.
盖博正在主持会议。

228
00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:51.660
He is outlining Saber's code of conduct, and it's super boring.
他正在宣读赛博公司的行为准则，超级无聊。

229
00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:57.560
If there's an award for fake yawn acting, I think I should receive it, because at 11
如果有一个假装打哈欠的演技奖，我觉得我应该拿奖，因为在11

230
00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:59.980
seconds, I do a real great fake yawn.
秒的时候，我表演了一个非常棒的假哈欠。

231
00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:00.840
Wow.
哇。

232
00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:01.380
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

233
00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:02.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

234
00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:05.520
But yeah, Kelly says, oh, my God, kill me.
然后凯莉说，天哪，杀了我吧。

235
00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:07.420
And Andy's like, hey, all right.
安迪说，嘿，行吧。

236
00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:10.560
Obviously, we all want to die, but we have to get through this.
显然，我们都想死，但我们必须熬过去。

237
00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:11.480
So, Gabe, go ahead.
所以，盖博，请继续。

238
00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:12.040
It's okay.
没关系。

239
00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:15.940
This is when Pam says, oh, I'm going into labor.
就在这时帕姆说，哦，我要生了。

240
00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:18.720
Which I guess she's been doing a lot.
我想她最近经常这么说。

241
00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:19.480
A lot.
经常。

242
00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:20.580
To get out of things.
为了逃避事情。

243
00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:22.580
So, no one believes her.
所以，没人相信她。

244
00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:23.080
No.
没有。

245
00:11:23.340 --> 00:11:24.960
They're like, you are not going into labor.
他们说，你根本没要生。

246
00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:29.040
But then, oh, my gosh, her water breaks.
但随后，天哪，她羊水破了。

247
00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.820
She really is going into labor.
她是真的要生了。

248
00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:32.620
And people are like, oh, my gosh, okay.
大家反应过来，天哪，好吧。

249
00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:34.780
Well, I mean, good luck.
我是说，祝你好运。

250
00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:35.600
We love you.
我们爱你。

251
00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:39.740
And then a water bottle falls out from between her legs.
然后一个水瓶从她两腿之间掉了出来。

252
00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:41.900
It's been duct taped to her thigh.
它被用大力胶粘在了她的大腿上。

253
00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:42.500
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

254
00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:43.760
Yeah, let me tell you about that.
是啊，让我跟你说说那件事。

255
00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:44.160
What?
什么？

256
00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:44.980
Let me tell you how we did this.
让我告诉你我们是怎么做到的。

257
00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:51.080
This was really tricky because I had to, and you can see me start to do it.
这真的很难，因为我必须……你可以看到我开始做那个动作了。

258
00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:55.660
I had that bottle duct taped to my thigh for real.
我当时真的用大力胶把那个瓶子粘在大腿上了。

259
00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:57.160
It was just some leggings.
外面就穿了条紧身裤。

260
00:11:57.540 --> 00:11:57.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

261
00:11:57.960 --> 00:11:58.200
Right?
对吧？

262
00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:04.200
And then I had to, like, kind of undo the lid to let the water out.
然后我得，怎么说呢，把盖子拧开一点让水流出来。

263
00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:05.560
How did you do that?
你是怎么做到的？

264
00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:07.400
I start, you see me start to do it.
我开始做了，你看到我开始做那个动作了。

265
00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:08.840
I kind of start to reach up.
我伸手去够了一下。

266
00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:09.420
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

267
00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:10.780
And then the puddle.
然后就是那滩水。

268
00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:11.440
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

269
00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:15.800
But then I had to also make the water bottle fall on the ground.
但之后我还得让水瓶掉到地上。

270
00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:21.780
So there's a cut because then as I'm shuffling out, we had to take the tape off.
所以中间剪辑了一下，因为当我挪步走出去的时候，我们得把胶带撕掉。

271
00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:23.740
There was no way to make it fall off.
没法让它自然掉下来。

272
00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:26.080
So we kind of took the tape off.
所以我们把胶带撕掉了。

273
00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:28.260
And then I'm just shuffling with this bottle.
然后我就带着这个瓶子挪步。

274
00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:34.140
I'm, like, holding it with my thighs until I'm supposed to kind of let it go onto the ground.
我用大腿夹着它，直到我该把它放掉落到地上为止。

275
00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:34.750
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

276
00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:38.300
It was a whole, like, we spent, we're like, wait, how are we doing this?
这真是个大工程，我们当时都在想，等等，我们要怎么做？

277
00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:41.200
How is this tape suddenly falling off?
这胶带怎么会突然掉下来？

278
00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.400
Add this to my fake award show.
把这个加进我的假颁奖典礼里。

279
00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:44.120
Thank you.
谢谢。

280
00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:45.000
For fake yawning.
颁给假装打哈欠。

281
00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:49.820
And then you get the award for stunt water bottle acting.
然后你获得了特技水瓶表演奖。

282
00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:52.940
I would love to see that on a plaque.
我很想在奖牌上看到这个奖项。

283
00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:53.980
Stunt water bottle.
特技水瓶奖。

284
00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:55.360
Water bottle acting goes to.
水瓶表演奖得主是。

285
00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:57.020
Who are the other nominees?
还有哪些提名者？

286
00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:58.720
Fake yawn goes to.
假装打哈欠奖得主是。

287
00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:01.180
But that was how we did it.
总之我们就是这么做的。

288
00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:01.980
You did a great job.
你做得太棒了。

289
00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:03.540
I had a lot of questions for Pam.
我当时对帕姆有很多疑问。

290
00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:08.340
Pam, I looked up, do people fake labor to get out of things?
帕姆，我查了一下，真的有人会假装临产来逃避事情吗？

291
00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:10.240
And it turns out people do.
结果发现还真有。

292
00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:11.620
I don't doubt it.
我对此深信不疑。

293
00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:15.080
I think Pam did it the most, though.
不过我觉得帕姆是做得最过分的。

294
00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:18.560
The episode is going to start with Andy on his phone.
这一集开头是安迪在打电话。

295
00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:22.080
He's loudly saying that he cannot believe what he's hearing.
他大声说着不敢相信自己听到了什么。

296
00:13:22.220 --> 00:13:23.600
Another client has been stolen.
又有一个客户被抢走了。

297
00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:25.620
It's like war out there.
外面简直就像战场一样。

298
00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.180
No one's listening.
没人听他的。

299
00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:35.560
Yes, he's trying to create a metaphor such that everyone will go to Gettysburg with him, basically.
是的，他试图制造一个隐喻，好让大家都跟他去葛底斯堡。

300
00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:38.940
He holds up a pamphlet at two minutes and 20 seconds.
他在两分二十秒的时候举起了一本小册子。

301
00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:40.460
Phil Shea made that pamphlet.
那本小册子是菲尔·谢伊做的。

302
00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:42.180
Well done, Phil Shea.
干得好，菲尔·谢伊。

303
00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:42.540
Yes.
没错。

304
00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:45.060
But yeah, Andy's trying to rally the troops.
不过确实，安迪正试图召集大家。

305
00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:45.960
What's that saying?
那句老话怎么说来着？

306
00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:48.540
Nothing brings people together like a common enemy.
没有什么比共同的敌人更能让人们团结在一起了。

307
00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:49.440
Yes.
是的。

308
00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:52.100
But Andy's trying to get a buzz going.
但安迪正试图制造点声势。

309
00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:52.860
He is.
他确实在这么做。

310
00:13:53.420 --> 00:14:00.140
Dwight is going to point out he has a beef, which is that everybody always talks about Gettysburg.
德怀特打算指出他有个心结，那就是每个人都在谈论葛底斯堡战役。

311
00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:00.520
Yeah.
是啊。

312
