You're like, I don't want to learn dragon names and blah, blah.
你之前不是说，不想去记什么龙的名字之类的吗。

534
00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:50.200
This is so different.
这完全不一样。

535
00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:52.320
These are two totally different kinds of movies.
这是两种完全不同类型的电影。

536
00:23:52.580 --> 00:23:54.160
How do you go into a human body?
他怎么进入别人身体的？

537
00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:58.980
And, like, what are these rules of physics I'm having to learn to make this movie make sense?
还有，为了让这部电影逻辑通顺，我得去学这些物理规则吗？

538
00:23:58.980 --> 00:24:00.980
Listen, I guess I love fantasy physics.
听着，我想我就是喜欢这种奇幻物理学。

539
00:24:01.220 --> 00:24:01.960
I guess you do.
看来你是挺喜欢的。

540
00:24:02.560 --> 00:24:03.760
Sass from you.
你还挺刻薄的。

541
00:24:03.880 --> 00:24:05.040
My gosh.
天哪。

542
00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:06.560
Hello.
你好。

543
00:24:07.580 --> 00:24:12.720
Speaking of sass, Macy T in Alberta has maybe some mini sass.
说到刻薄，阿尔伯塔省的梅西·T可能也有点小刻薄。

544
00:24:12.920 --> 00:24:13.840
Let's hear it, Macy.
让我们听听看，梅西。

545
00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:15.100
Macy says,
梅西说，

546
00:24:15.100 --> 00:24:18.780
It has always bothered me that when they arrive at Gettysburg, it looks like it's evening.
一直以来让我困扰的是，当他们到达葛底斯堡时，看起来像是傍晚。

547
00:24:19.060 --> 00:24:23.620
There are long shadows and the orange sunlight hitting the side of their faces in the bus.
车里有长长的影子，橙色的阳光照在他们脸的一侧。

548
00:24:23.820 --> 00:24:26.820
But then when they get off the bus, it looks like normal daytime.
但当他们下车时，看起来又像是正常的白天。

549
00:24:27.360 --> 00:24:29.260
Was the arrival filmed in the evening?
到达的那一幕是在傍晚拍摄的吗？

550
00:24:29.400 --> 00:24:32.160
And how many days did it take to film all the Gettysburg parts?
拍摄所有葛底斯堡的戏份一共花了多少天？

551
00:24:32.480 --> 00:24:34.220
Macy is paying attention.
梅西很专注。

552
00:24:34.920 --> 00:24:35.840
That's for sure.
那是肯定的。

553
00:24:36.420 --> 00:24:39.800
Well, according to Steve Burgess, we shot two days at Woodley Park.
嗯，据史蒂夫·伯吉斯所说，我们在伍德利公园拍了两天。

554
00:24:40.260 --> 00:24:41.040
And Steve said,
史蒂夫说，

555
00:24:41.220 --> 00:24:43.380
Unfortunately, sometimes we had to shoot out of order.
很遗憾，有时我们不得不打乱顺序拍摄。

556
00:24:43.380 --> 00:24:45.580
And so the shadows do not match.
所以影子对不上。

557
00:24:46.380 --> 00:24:48.940
And he said that this made Matt Soane crazy.
他说这让马特·索恩快疯了。

558
00:24:49.180 --> 00:24:50.480
But we didn't have any choice.
但我们别无选择。

559
00:24:50.740 --> 00:24:52.060
This is how we had to do it.
我们只能这么做。

560
00:24:52.600 --> 00:24:55.280
Macy, Matt Soane would have talked your ear off about this.
梅西，马特·索恩要是听到这个肯定会跟你唠叨个没完。

561
00:24:55.540 --> 00:24:56.100
That's right.
没错。

562
00:24:56.320 --> 00:24:58.000
I thought that was a really good catch.
我觉得这观察得很到位。

563
00:24:58.100 --> 00:24:58.680
I do, too.
我也这么觉得。

564
00:24:58.680 --> 00:24:59.060
Good attention to detail.
细节关注得很好。

565
00:24:59.200 --> 00:24:59.700
I do, too.
我也是。

566
00:25:00.020 --> 00:25:02.440
Well, as the group is approaching the visitor center,
嗯，当团队接近游客中心时，

567
00:25:02.660 --> 00:25:04.260
Andy blocks them because he's like,
安迪拦住了他们，因为他觉得，

568
00:25:04.320 --> 00:25:05.420
Hey, we're not tourists.
嘿，我们可不是游客。

569
00:25:06.040 --> 00:25:08.720
We are going to do the Andy Bernard tour.
我们要进行安迪·伯纳德式的游览。

570
00:25:08.720 --> 00:25:09.940
Oh, no.
噢，不。

571
00:25:10.260 --> 00:25:10.580
Yeah.
是啊。

572
00:25:10.840 --> 00:25:11.040
Yeah.
没错。

573
00:25:11.480 --> 00:25:11.820
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

574
00:25:12.420 --> 00:25:14.160
Well, when Andy starts his tour,
嗯，当安迪开始他的游览时，

575
00:25:14.780 --> 00:25:16.420
Dwight is in the background,
德怀特在背景里，

576
00:25:16.420 --> 00:25:21.560
and he is kind of schooling Aaron on the Battle of Shroot Farms,
他正在给亚伦科普关于施鲁特农场之战的事，

577
00:25:21.660 --> 00:25:24.720
which he again says the history books have ignored.
他再次强调历史书忽略了这场战役。

578
00:25:25.060 --> 00:25:25.180
Right.
对。

579
00:25:25.180 --> 00:25:28.800
You should see some of these letters that the soldiers wrote about their time there.
你应该看看那些士兵写下的关于在那段时光的信件。

580
00:25:28.940 --> 00:25:34.880
And once again, it is the northernmost battle of the Civil War.
再一次重申，这是内战中最北端的战役。

581
00:25:35.700 --> 00:25:40.240
Well, you know, when Dwight was telling Aaron she should read some of the letters from the soldiers,
嗯，你知道，当德怀特告诉亚伦她应该读读士兵们的信件时，

582
00:25:40.700 --> 00:25:43.400
this made me think about a time where I was in a museum,
这让我想起有次我去博物馆，

583
00:25:43.400 --> 00:25:47.320
and they would have letters from long ago displayed in glass cases,
他们把很久以前的信件展示在玻璃柜里，

584
00:25:47.320 --> 00:25:50.300
and you could read, like, what people were doing at the time.
你可以读到当时人们在做什么。

585
00:25:50.300 --> 00:25:53.240
So, I looked online, and the New York State Library,
所以我上网查了一下，纽约州立图书馆，

586
00:25:53.480 --> 00:25:58.540
in commemoration of the 150th anniversary of two major Civil War battles,
为了纪念两场重大内战战役的150周年，

587
00:25:58.820 --> 00:26:00.880
including Gettysburg and Vicksburg,
包括葛底斯堡战役和维克斯堡战役，

588
00:26:01.820 --> 00:26:05.360
digitized some of the letters from the soldiers and put them on their website.
将一些士兵的信件数字化并放到了他们的网站上。

589
00:26:05.660 --> 00:26:06.240
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

590
00:26:06.520 --> 00:26:06.740
Yeah.
是啊。

591
00:26:06.740 --> 00:26:10.020
So, you don't have to go to a museum to see some of these.
所以，你不需要去博物馆就能看到这些信件。

592
00:26:10.240 --> 00:26:11.320
You can go on their website.
你可以直接上他们的网站看。

593
00:26:11.320 --> 00:26:12.440
I'll put it in stories.
我会把它发到快拍里。

594
00:26:12.640 --> 00:26:14.460
I found them very fascinating.
我觉得它们非常迷人。

595
00:26:14.720 --> 00:26:15.880
I want to read one.
我想读一封。

596
00:26:16.180 --> 00:26:16.420
Okay.
好的。

597
00:26:17.200 --> 00:26:18.820
This is from Calvin A.
这封信来自卡尔文·A·

598
00:26:18.980 --> 00:26:19.420
Haynes,
海恩斯，

599
00:26:19.540 --> 00:26:23.760
who served as a sergeant in the 125th New York Infantry.
他曾在纽约第125步兵团担任中士。

600
00:26:24.060 --> 00:26:26.100
He was raised in Troy, New York,
他在纽约特洛伊长大，

601
00:26:26.120 --> 00:26:30.280
and he has written a letter to his wife about the Battle of Gettysburg.
他写了一封信给妻子，讲述了葛底斯堡战役。

602
00:26:31.180 --> 00:26:33.400
July 19th, 1863.
1863年7月19日。

603
00:26:33.920 --> 00:26:34.880
Dear wife.
亲爱的妻子。

604
00:26:36.740 --> 00:26:37.400
I'm sorry.
我很抱歉。

605
00:26:37.780 --> 00:26:39.320
Just wait for the first line.
先等等，看第一行。

606
00:26:39.880 --> 00:26:42.320
Not having heard from you in a great while,
许久没有你的消息，

607
00:26:42.320 --> 00:26:45.300
I did not know but what you would like to hear,
我不知道你是否想知道，

608
00:26:45.520 --> 00:26:46.920
whether I am dead or alive.
我是死是活。

609
00:26:47.180 --> 00:26:47.960
Oh, no.
噢，不。

610
00:26:48.180 --> 00:26:49.920
Something is happening in this marriage.
这段婚姻出问题了。

611
00:26:49.940 --> 00:26:50.360
I know.
我知道。

612
00:26:50.440 --> 00:26:51.020
Very clear.
非常清楚。

613
00:26:51.200 --> 00:26:52.880
Just the beginning, opening beginning,
仅仅是开头，刚开始的开头，

614
00:26:53.060 --> 00:26:54.580
made me think of that SNL sketch,
就让我想起了那个《周六夜现场》的小品，

615
00:26:54.760 --> 00:26:55.440
Dear Lydia,
亲爱的莉迪亚，

616
00:26:56.000 --> 00:26:57.080
where he's writing just,
他写信的那段，

617
00:26:57.400 --> 00:26:58.700
Oh, my gosh, it's so good.
天哪，真是太棒了。

618
00:26:58.840 --> 00:26:58.980
Okay.
好吧。

619
00:26:59.340 --> 00:27:01.680
Anyway, Calvin goes on to say,
总之，卡尔文接着写道，

620
00:27:02.360 --> 00:27:04.240
I am enjoying good health at present.
我目前身体状况良好。

621
00:27:04.240 --> 00:27:08.200
We have had an awful march and a terrible battle.
我们经历了一场艰苦的行军和一场惨烈的战斗。

622
00:27:08.500 --> 00:27:11.560
A great many of our boys were killed or wounded,
我们很多弟兄阵亡或受伤了，

623
00:27:11.620 --> 00:27:13.580
but I escaped without a scratch.
但我毫发无伤地逃过一劫。

624
00:27:13.800 --> 00:27:16.920
It is a miracle that we were not all killed or wounded.
我们没全军覆没简直是个奇迹。

625
00:27:17.180 --> 00:27:19.200
We were in the thickest of the fight,
我们当时身处激战中心，

626
00:27:19.340 --> 00:27:21.300
making a charge on the Rebs,
向叛军发起冲锋，

627
00:27:21.980 --> 00:27:25.600
a half a mile through a fire of grape and canister.
在半英里的葡萄弹和榴霰弹火网中穿行。

628
00:27:26.240 --> 00:27:29.560
Our regiment lost 100 men in 10 minutes.
我们团在10分钟内损失了100人。

629
00:27:30.160 --> 00:27:33.020
Our company lost 8 and 14 were wounded.
我们连有8人阵亡，14人受伤。

630
00:27:33.820 --> 00:27:35.780
Stephen Hunt was wounded in the hip.
斯蒂芬·亨特臀部中弹。

